implementationPlan.description:
Verification gate. Run the ONE verification command below exactly once, after the last edit, with run_in_background. Its fresh output is the complete_task evidence, and QA re-runs it verbatim. It takes about 40 minutes: postflight.sh, then postflight.ps1 on PS 5.1 and on pwsh 7.

What the command does:
- snapshots HEAD's scripts/ into /mnt/d/moe-scratch/t4fdc-XXXX and copies the 4 changed scripts over, cmp-verified;
- unsets leaked MOE_/CLAUDE/FAKE_ env and checks that ci.yml parses;
- runs bash -n;
- on both engines: ParseFile of moe-agent.ps1 and landing-ledger.ps1, then landing-ledger.ps1 itself;
- runs parity-check.sh and parity-check.ps1 (PS 5.1);
- runs the three postflight test runs with MOE_POSTFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SEC=180;
- writes <dir>.log, ending in GATE_EXIT=<n>.

Poll with `until grep -q '^GATE_EXIT=' "$(cat /tmp/t4fdc-dir).log"; do sleep 20; done`. The foreground cap is 600 s, so re-poll.

Pass means all of:
- GATE_EXIT=0;
- '[landing-ledger powershell.exe] ok' and '[landing-ledger pwsh.exe] ok';
- '[scenario AJ1] ok' and '[scenario AJ2] ok' in all three postflight runs;
- the same scope counts as before: sh 42, ps1 41, or one fewer or one more as symlink support differs.

Do not edit any file while the gate runs. If a ps1 failure looks environmental, rerun the parent revision's scripts the same way before blaming the change (Serena gotcha-qa-ps1-postflight-from-wsl).

Full postflight regression is warranted on this mid-epic task because the change touches every ps1 landing's ledger path.

COMMAND:
cd /mnt/d/projexts/moes && W=$(mktemp -d /mnt/d/moe-scratch/t4fdc-XXXX) && echo "$W" > /tmp/t4fdc-dir && ( for v in $(compgen -e | grep -E '^(MOE_|CLAUDE|FAKE_)'); do unset "$v"; done; git rev-parse HEAD && python3 -I -c 'import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open(".github/workflows/ci.yml"))' && echo "[ci.yml] ok" && git archive HEAD scripts | tar -x -C "$W" && for f in scripts/moe-agent.ps1 scripts/tests/landing-ledger.ps1 scripts/tests/postflight.sh scripts/tests/postflight.ps1; do cp "$f" "$W/$f" && cmp "$f" "$W/$f" || exit 1; done && cd "$W" && bash -n scripts/moe-agent.sh && echo "[bash -n] ok" && for eng in powershell.exe pwsh.exe; do for s in scripts/moe-agent.ps1 scripts/tests/landing-ledger.ps1; do P="$(wslpath -w "$W/$s")"; $eng -NoProfile -Command "\$e=\$null; [void][System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseFile('$P',[ref]\$null,[ref]\$e); exit \$e.Count" && echo "[ParseFile $eng $s] ok" || exit 1; done; $eng -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$(wslpath -w "$W/scripts/tests/landing-ledger.ps1")" && echo "[landing-ledger $eng] ok" || exit 1; done && bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh && echo "[parity-check.sh] ok" && powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$(wslpath -w "$W/scripts/tests/parity-check.ps1")" && echo "[parity-check.ps1 PS5.1] ok" && echo "=== Linux bash postflight.sh ===" && MOE_POSTFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SEC=180 bash scripts/tests/postflight.sh && echo "=== Windows PowerShell 5.1 postflight.ps1 ===" && WSLENV=MOE_POSTFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SEC MOE_POSTFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SEC=180 powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$(wslpath -w "$W/scripts/tests/postflight.ps1")" && echo "=== pwsh 7 postflight.ps1 ===" && WSLENV=MOE_POSTFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SEC MOE_POSTFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SEC=180 pwsh.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$(wslpath -w "$W/scripts/tests/postflight.ps1")" ) > "$W.log" 2>&1; echo "GATE_EXIT=$?" >> "$W.log"; echo "$W"
